WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.280
Auckland International Airport

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.080
processes 21 million passengers
every year and climbing.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.560
Customs and Immigration
have just been alerted to a visiting

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.920
Lithuanian woman with quite a history.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.480
Officer James is keen to take on the case.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.760
It looks like she had some trouble
in the US on en route to New Zealand.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.320
She's coming out of UK

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.760
so I'm going to have a talk with her
and see what interactions she had

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.040
with the US authorities
en route to New Zealand.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.360
I need to ask you your reasons

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.640
for coming to New Zealand
as well as what happened over in the USA.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:12.000
The woman tries to front foot
her situation by producing correspondence

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.640
with New Zealand authorities
to avoid delay.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.920
You see that you needed 
to have a visa for New Zealand

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.960
and you have a very important
family events here in New Zealand.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.960
Indeed, actually,
I'm visiting my boyfriend

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.160
who actually who lives
in New Zealand. Oh, great.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:27.640
But I just

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.880
want to make sure that I can call you
from an immigration perspective.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.600
Lithuanian nationals can travel
to New Zealand as visitors without a visa.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.200
But James wants to know
that she's not here to disappear.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.040
Can I.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.680
Can I ask
how long you were living in the USA?

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:49.080
For like 17, 18 years.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.560
Seventeen years?

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.760
Eighteen years?
And what Visa did you hold?

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.600
What Visa were you holding?

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:59.800
Um, I was, the Visa um,
I was issued the Visa over 20 years ago

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.920
I don’t exactly remember
a truly specific Visa that was issued.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.640
James knows she's lying.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.120
His American counterparts have
already told him she's never had a U.S.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.840
visa. What about USA?

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.800
What about USA?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.240
Yeah, what happened in the USA?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.240
At Auckland’s Air Cargo facility,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:25.560
Customs officer Hayden believes
this parcel is worth checking out.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.560
So we've identified a consignment here
that we believe is suspicious.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.840
It's come from
West Africa, the country of Mali.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.760
It's been declared as motor parts

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.800
worth 300,000 NZD, which is quite high
considering the site of the consignment.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.000
There doesn't seem to be any padding
or protection for it.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.320
It's hard to imagine what car parts
could be worth $300,000,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.280
let alone why the exporters
were keen to get them here so quickly.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:56.080
They agreed to pay 60 grand in customs
charges for the privilege.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.640
The items that are inside
are very poorly packaged.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.960
You'd expect there
to be some packaging material

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.640
or some sort of order to the way
that they package, but it just doesn't.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.640
It looks like they've 
just been thrown in there together

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.280
and for something worth so much.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.440
Yeah, the alarm bells are definitely
ringing here.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.080
There’s some organic material here
of some kind, um, that doesn’t fit

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.200
the description of motor vehicle parts,

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.720
we just wouldn’t expect
to find organic material in there.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.080
The Republic of Mali seems to feature
highly optimistic car park dealers.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.880
The parts are worth a fraction 
of even the shipping cost. 

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.000
This is the sort of product

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.200
you could pick up at your local parts
store in New Zealand for

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.320
a small amount of money.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.480
It's just not consistent
with the valuation.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.440
I'm not a mechanic,
but I would expect this area

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.560
here to be free moving.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.680
It looks like a bearing of some kind,
but it's rock solid.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.320
So again, alarm 
bells are definitely ringing here.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.160
Hayden's no mechanic,
but he knows how to swing a hammer.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.200
That's broken the metal straight off.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.520
So, again,not not 
something you'd expect from a part

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:01.720
so expensive.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.160
While Hayden had his bearings

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.440
right, the manufacturers didn’t.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:10.440
Hello, what do we have here?

